From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:11:59 -0400
Subject: feat: the sidebar comes back whatever On startup says (S-323)

GitHub issue 43, the owner's call of 2026-10-30: a launch brings back
each normal window's essentials, Space pins and folders whatever On
startup says, and the choice decides the loose tabs alone, as in Arc.
With the New Tab page or specific pages the launch now restores the
session with RESTORE_SIDEBAR_ONLY, which drops the loose tabs, popups
and windows left empty before any browser is made, and adds the New
Tab page or the pages. Chromium's own pinned-tab list is not opened as
well, which would double the essentials. The Mac's Dock and the
no-window restore follow the same rule. The archive marks only the
tabs that come back; the loose ones carry a mark of their own and stay
rows.

Why: GitHub issue 43; the owner asked on 2026-10-30 for the sidebar to come
back whatever On startup says.
Removable when: never as a feature; the startup and restore hunks go if
Chromium restores pinned tabs with their place and folders on its own.
